Well, I find it hard to care about "making it too easy" for the highly
skilled player, when I'm not there and won't be for some time.  I find
that using shopkeepers to ID stuff grants an unfair advantage to the
highly experienced players *anyway* -- randomize *everything*, including
prices, and you'd more than offset "making it too easy", I think.

Should I get to the point where I was a highly skilled player, perhaps
I'd look at it differently.

