I actually don't see a problem with the conducts for those wishing for
more of a 'real challenge'.  I'm all for adding *more* conducts, and
for declaring conducts before gameplay begins (and failing makes the
game "unwinnable", like changing alignment too soon).

I'm actually suprised you think an additional altar would be that 
unbalancing to the game.   And frankly, I don't follow your reasoning
*why* -- especially with stuff like being able to use shopkeepers to
ID items in the game: that lets the "highly skilled" (experienced)
players have an advantage that the unspoiled or newbie players don't.

This isn't to say that I'm claiming you're wrong about the balance
issue.  I just don't follow how it would be so damaging. Amplification
would be welcome. :)

